      "text": "The identity \\(\\tan(x+y) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan y}{1 - \\tan x \\tan y}\\) states that to find \\(\\tan\\left(x + \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\), we must substitute \\(\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\) for \\(y\\). If we write this out, we get:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) &= \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{3}{-1} = -3\n\\end{align*}Thus, we conclude that \\(\\tan\\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\boxed{-3}\\).",
