      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We can use the identity $\\tan(x+y) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan y}{1 - \\tan x \\tan y}$. Substituting $y$ with $\\frac{\\pi}{4},$ we have $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}.$\n\nSimplifying, we get $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + 1}{1 - \\tan x}.$\n\nSubstituting $\\tan x = 2,$ we have $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2} = \\boxed{-3}.$\n\nThus, the answer is -3.",
