    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We can use the trigonometric identity for tangent of a sum to solve this problem. The identity gives us:\n\n$$\\tan(a + b) = \\frac{\\tan a + \\tan b}{1 - \\tan a \\tan b}$$\n\nWe need to find $\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)$, so we can apply this identity.\n\n$\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}$\n\nSubstitute $\\tan x = 2$ and $\\tan \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = 1$:\n\n$\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2 \\cdot 1}$\n\nSimplifying this expression gives:\n\n$\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{3}{-1} = \\boxed{-3}$",
