    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Since the tangent is periodic with period $\\pi,$ we have $\\tan x = \\tan \\left( x + \\pi \\right),$ so\n\\begin{align*}\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) &= \\tan \\left( x + \\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) \\\\\n&= \\tan \\left( x + \\frac{3 \\pi}{4} \\right) \\\\\n&= \\tan \\left( x - \\frac{3 \\pi}{4} \\right) \\\\\n&= -\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{3 \\pi}{4} \\right) \\\\\n&= -\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) \\\\\n&= \\boxed{-2}.\n\\end{align*}. The answer is \\boxed{-2}.Can you think of an organized argument that logically leads to the answer?",
